# Git commits

When proposing or writing git commit messages (including multi-line bodies):

- Do **not** append `Made-with: Cursor`, `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, or similar tool attribution lines unless the user explicitly asks for them.
- Keep the subject line and body focused on the change; end the body without marketing or editor metadata.

This applies to commits created via the agent, suggested commit messages, and `git commit -m` content.

## Repository tooling (humans on this repo)

After cloning, run once so Git strips any injected `Made-with: Cursor` line and uses the shared template for `git commit` (no `-m`):

`git config core.hooksPath .githooks`

`git config commit.template .gitmessage`

Also disable Cursor commit attribution in the app: **Cursor Settings → Agent → Attribution**.
